      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 1 · Day 1\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 1\n- Day: 1\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L1\n- Lesson Role: Unit opener and Vocabulary 1 presentation\n\n## Day Focus\n- Introduce the first vocabulary set for friends and family (man, woman, boy, girl, family) through the Power Up café scene.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Friends and family (light chat — who lives with you?)\n- Song: The More We Get Together (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 1\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners can listen to, identify, and join in saying the lesson words with teacher support.\n- Source: TB p8 | PB p8 | AB p8 | Audio 1.01, 1.02, 1.03, AB 1.01\n- New Keywords: man, woman, boy, girl, family, café, find, friend, new\n- Recycled Keywords: colours, numbers, bird, boat, book, crayon\n- Target Sentences: Is (Jenny) a (girl)? | Who's this?\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Listen and point to the PB p8 café scene; meet Jim, Jenny and Cameron.\n  2. Guided Practice — Friends and Family flashcard presentation + hidden-bird picture hunt (\"Find the bird\").\n  3. Game / Application — Two-group chant \"Man, woman, boy, girl / Family\" and a face-down flashcard game.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Family Book (Todd Parr) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 1): Picture walk — explore cover and illustrations, predict, notice that families can look different.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: man, woman, boy, girl, family, café, find, friend, new, Is (Jenny) a (girl)?, Who's this?\n- Original Recycled Language: colours, numbers, bird, boat, book, crayon, What's colour's this?, What's number's this?\n- Current Classification Result: New / recycled split carried from source; family included in Day 1 New Keywords per unit Language Bank (source also lists it as New Language).\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - colours\n  - numbers\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
