      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 1 · Day 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 1\n- Day: 2\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L2\n- Lesson Role: Language presentation and practice 1\n\n## Day Focus\n- Ask and answer about name and age using the Power Up characters.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Names and ages (light chat — what's your name? how old are you?)\n- Song: The More We Get Together (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 1\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners can respond to questions about their name and age with a name, number, or supported phrase.\n- Source: TB p9 | PB p9 | AB p9 | Audio 1.04, 1.05, AB 1.02, 1.03\n- New Keywords: What's your name? | My name's (Anna). | How old are you? | I'm (six). | Jenny's (five). | twins\n- Recycled Keywords: colours, numbers, objects, I'm (Jenny/Jim). | Who's this?\n- Target Sentences: What's your name? | My name's (Anna). | How old are you? | I'm (six). | Jenny's (five).\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Meet the characters and their ages (Jim, Jenny, Matt, Anna, Cameron); listen to the name-and-age dialogue.\n  2. Guided Practice — Find-and-point / hide-and-find using character cards and ages.\n  3. Game / Application — \"What's your name?\" circle; children respond with a name or a number (not a full sentence required).\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Family Book (Todd Parr) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 2): Join in — listen to the refrain, point to pictures, chant along with teacher support.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: What's your name? | My name's (Anna). | How old are you? | I'm (six). | Jenny's (five). | twins\n- Original Recycled Language: colours, numbers, objects, I'm (Jenny/Jim)., Who's this?\n- Current Classification Result: New / recycled split carried from source; twins treated as identify-only (no forced output).\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - colours\n  - numbers\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
