      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 1 · Day 4\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 1\n- Day: 4\n- Day Type: Media Extend\n- Power Up Lesson: — (EASTIE extension, no Power Up page)\n- Lesson Role: EASTIE-added Media Extend\n\n## Day Focus\n- Extend the week's family theme through a themed media input and a simple shared artefact.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Our families (light chat — who is in your family?)\n- Song: The More We Get Together (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 1\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners can point to people in a family portrait and use familiar words or supported phrases to introduce them.\n- Source: Media Extend 1 (EASTIE-added; design pending — see Unit Open Items)\n- New Keywords: — (none new; consolidates Week 1 friend / family words)\n- Recycled Keywords: man, woman, boy, girl, family, mum, dad, brother, sister, pet\n- Target Sentences: Who's this? | This is my ... (familiar phrases from prior days)\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Media Input — Watch Peppa Pig, \"Mummy Pig's Birthday\" (Season 1, ~5 min; family prepares a birthday surprise for Mummy Pig). Thematically linked to the week's friends-and-family theme. Fallback if unavailable: a Bluey family episode.\n  2. Guided Practice — Make a simple family portrait using the week's words.\n  3. Game / Application — Prepare the portrait as the Day 5 Mini Mission artefact.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Family Book (Todd Parr) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 4): Own-life link — connect the book's ideas to the child's own family; supports the Day 4 family portrait.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: — (EASTIE extension, no Power Up source page)\n- Original Recycled Language: Week 1 friend / family words (carried forward)\n- Current Classification Result: Media Extend slot; media locked as Peppa Pig \"Mummy Pig's Birthday\" (family-themed), Bluey as fallback. Artefact format (family portrait) stays a teacher-design choice.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - Artefact format for the family portrait (teacher-design choice; media clip itself is locked)\n- Source Issues:\n  - Media Extend 1 marked \"Waiting for teacher design\" in source.\n",
