      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 1 · Day 5\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 1\n- Day: 5\n- Day Type: Mini Mission\n- Power Up Lesson: — (EASTIE extension, no Power Up page)\n- Lesson Role: EASTIE-added Mini Mission\n\n## Day Focus\n- Share the family portrait in a supportive, celebration-style mini mission.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: What we learned about families (light chat before the mission)\n- Song: The More We Get Together (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 1\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners can share a family portrait by pointing, naming one family member, or using a supported \"This is my ...\" phrase.\n- Source: Mini Mission 1 (EASTIE-added; design pending — see Unit Open Items)\n- New Keywords: — (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: man, woman, boy, girl, family, mum, dad, brother, sister, pet\n- Target Sentences: Who's this? | This is my family. | This is my mum / dad / brother / sister / pet.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Display the Day 4 family portraits on a class family wall.\n  2. Guided Practice — Each child shares their portrait; peers ask \"Who's this?\"; teacher supports \"This is my ...\".\n  3. Game / Application — Build the class family wall; position the mission as celebration and sharing, not testing.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Family Book (Todd Parr) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 5): Retell — recall the book with support; child retells a favourite page using familiar words.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: — (EASTIE extension)\n- Original Recycled Language: Week 1 friend / family words\n- Current Classification Result: Mini Mission slot; positioned as celebration / share, not assessment.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - Mission language scaffold (open — see Unit Open Items)\n- Source Issues:\n  - Mini Mission 1 marked \"Waiting for teacher design\" in source.\n",
