      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 2 · Day 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 2\n- Day: 2\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L5\n- Lesson Role: Literature — story focus (Home Time Story)\n\n## Day Focus\n- Listen to the real-life Home Time Story and meet school-life words (school, home, sit down, teacher, they're).\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Going to school and going home — when do we sit down? who is our teacher?\n- Song: If You're Happy (Super Simple Songs, 09. 情绪情感) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 2\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners listen to a real-life story about home time and understand the key school-life words.\n- Source: TB p12 | PB p12 | AB p12 | Audio 1.11\n- New Keywords: (at) school, home, home time, sit down, teacher, Are they ... ?, They're ...\n- Recycled Keywords: friends and family, numbers\n- Target Sentences: Are they (at school)? | They're (at school).\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Listen to the Home Time Story; pause on \"sit down\", \"teacher\", \"home time\"; act them out.\n  2. Guided Practice — \"School or home?\" sorting: show a picture (classroom / house), learners call \"At school!\" or \"Home!\"; build They're ... sentences with support.\n  3. Game / Application — Role-play home time: one child is the teacher (\"Sit down, please\"), others act coming to school / going home; recycle happy from later in the week.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: Our Class is a Family (Shannon Olsen) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 2): Join in — read aloud with the class; invite learners to call out the repeated line and copy the classroom routines shown in the book (sit down, listen, help).\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (at) school, home, home time, sit down, teacher, Are they ... ?, They're...\n- Original Recycled Language: friends and family, numbers\n- Current Classification Result: New / recycled split carried from source.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - friends and family (recycled anchor for the story)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
