      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 2 · Day 3\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 2\n- Day: 3\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L6\n- Lesson Role: Literature — response to story and mid-unit evaluation\n\n## Day Focus\n- Recognise the emotion happy in the story and show understanding through a simple response activity (mid-unit check-in).\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: What makes us happy at school? (recycles friend / teacher / sit down)\n- Song: If You're Happy (Super Simple Songs, 09. 情绪情感) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 2\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners recognise the emotion happy in the story and show they understood it.\n- Source: TB p13 | AB p13 | Audio 1.08, 1.09\n- New Keywords: happy\n- Recycled Keywords: language from the story (school, home, teacher, sit down, friends and family)\n- Target Sentences: (He's / She's) happy. | Are they happy?\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Re-read the Home Time Story; pause on happy faces; learners make a happy face and point to happy characters.\n  2. Guided Practice — \"Happy or not?\" : show story frames, learners signal happy / not happy and say \"Happy!\"; link to He's / She's happy from Day 6.\n  3. Game / Application — Mid-unit check-in: each child draws or points to something that makes them happy at school; teacher notes understanding (no graded test).\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: Our Class is a Family (Shannon Olsen) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 3): Connect — link the book to this week's words: our class family is happy at school; point out school / teacher / sit down moments in the illustrations.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: happy\n- Original Recycled Language: language from the story\n- Current Classification Result: happy is the single new word; everything else is recycled from Days 6–7.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - happy as an emotion word (anchor for Showcase week mood)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
