      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 2 · Day 4\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 2\n- Day: 4\n- Day Type: Media Extend\n- Power Up Lesson: Media Extend 2\n- Lesson Role: EASTIE-added Media Extend — real-life screen input\n\n## Day Focus\n- Watch a short Peppa Pig clip about a first day at playgroup and connect it to this week's friends / school / happy words.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: First days and new friends (recycles friend, boy, girl, happy)\n- Song: If You're Happy (Super Simple Songs, 09. 情绪情感) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 2\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners watch a real-life cartoon clip and understand the gist (friends at school, a teacher, feeling happy).\n- Source: Peppa Pig, \"The Playgroup\" (Season 1, Episode 6, ~5 min) — George's first day at Peppa's playgroup; Madame Gazelle is the teacher, the children sit down to paint, and George is welcomed by his new friends. Focus words: friend, school, teacher, sit down, happy.\n- New Keywords: (none new — clip recycles Week 2 words)\n- Recycled Keywords: friend, boy, girl, school, teacher, sit down, happy, family\n- Target Sentences: He's / She's (happy). | Are they (friends)?\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Watch the clip; pause on \"sit down\" and the painting moment; learners act sit down and point to the teacher.\n  2. Guided Practice — \"Who is happy?\" after viewing: learners point to George / Peppa / the friends and say \"Happy!\"; link to Day 8 happy.\n  3. Game / Application — \"My first day\" circle: a few learners share a real first-day memory (with support); connect to George's first day and our class family.\n- Fallback if clip unavailable: a Bluey school / new-friends episode (e.g., a kinder-first-day story) used the same way.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: Our Class is a Family (Shannon Olsen) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 4): Own-life link — compare the playgroup in the clip to our own class family; talk about a friend or teacher who helps us, just like in the book.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — Media Extend recycles unit language)\n- Original Recycled Language: friend, school, teacher, sit down, happy, family\n- Current Classification Result: Media Extend is input-only; no new graded vocabulary, all words already in Weeks 1–2.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - real-life screen input as a listening scaffold\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
