      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 2 · Day 5\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 2\n- Day: 5\n- Day Type: Mini Mission\n- Power Up Lesson: Mini Mission 2\n- Lesson Role: EASTIE-added Mini Mission — apply the week's language\n\n## Day Focus\n- Apply Week 2 language in a small group \"happy friends\" task and close the week with the class-family story.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Our Week 2 friends — what did we learn? (recycles he / she, happy, friend)\n- Song: If You're Happy (Super Simple Songs, 09. 情绪情感) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 2 (final sing of the week)\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners use he / she, happy and friend words in a short group task with teacher support.\n- Source: Mini Mission 2 (EASTIE-designed) — builds on L4–L6 + Media Extend 2.\n- New Keywords: (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: He's / She's, happy, friend, school, teacher, sit down, boy, girl\n- Target Sentences: He's / She's (happy). | (Name) is my friend.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Warm-up — Quick \"happy friends\" chant recycling He's / She's (happy) about classmates.\n  2. Mission — In groups of 3–4, learners make a \"Happy Friends\" mini-poster: draw 2–3 friends, label boy / girl, add a happy face; each group shows and says one sentence (e.g., \"She's Anna. She's happy.\").\n  3. Share & close — Groups display posters; class says \"Well done!\"; teacher keeps them for the Week 4 Showcase wall.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: TBD (see Unit Open Items — phonics explicit from Week 3)\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: Our Class is a Family (Shannon Olsen) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 5): Retell — with teacher support, learners retell the book in one line (\"Our class is a family\") and point to their favourite spread; close the week by singing the song together.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — Mission consolidates Week 2)\n- Original Recycled Language: He's/She's, happy, friend, school, teacher, sit down, boy, girl\n- Current Classification Result: Mission is application-only; all language recycled from Week 2.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - group speaking confidence\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
