      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 3 · Day 1\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 3\n- Day: 1\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L7\n- Lesson Role: Phonics and Literacy (initial sounds b, c, m)\n\n## Day Focus\n- Introduce initial letter sounds b, c and m and meet the word menu in a café / food context.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Sounds around us — words that start with b / c / m (recycles boy, cat, mum from Week 1)\n- Song: Peekaboo, I Love You (Super Simple Songs, 11. 游戏儿歌) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 3\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners recognise initial letter sounds b, c and m and meet the word menu.\n- Source: TB p14 | PB p14 | AB p14 | Audio 1.12, 1.13, 1.14, AB 1.10, 1.11, 1.12\n- New Keywords: menu (Phonics focus sounds: b — boy / book; c — cat / café; m — mum / Matt / menu)\n- Recycled Keywords: blue, book, boy, brother, café, Cameron, cat, Matt, mum\n- Target Sentences: (sound play only — /b/ /c/ /m/; no full sentences at K1 phonics)\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Meet letter friends b, c, m; listen to the sound and watch the mouth; find them in menu, boy, cat, mum.\n  2. Guided Practice — Sound sort: hold up a picture (book / cat / mum), learners call the initial sound /b/ /c/ /m/.\n  3. Game / Application — \"Sound hunt\": around the café scene, find things starting with b, c, m (boy, book, cat, café, mum, menu); link menu to the café from Week 1.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Explicit this week — initial sounds b, c, m. Day 1 introduces all three with the anchor words boy, book (b); cat, café (c); mum, Matt, menu (m). Sound play only; no letter writing required at K1.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Great Big Book of Families (Mary Hoffman) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 1): Picture walk — explore the cover and the many different families; predict what families do together; notice homes, schools and pets.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: menu\n- Original Recycled Language: blue, book, boy, brother, café, Cameron, cat, Matt, mum\n- Current Classification Result: menu is the only new word; b/c/m phonics uses recycled vocabulary as anchors.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - initial sound discrimination (b vs m)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
