      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 3 · Day 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 3\n- Day: 2\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L8\n- Lesson Role: Cross-curricular and consolidation (family trees)\n\n## Day Focus\n- Learn about family trees and name grandma and grandpa; connect to the big book of families.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Who is in your family? (recycles mum, dad, brother, sister, family from Week 1)\n- Song: Peekaboo, I Love You (Super Simple Songs, 11. 游戏儿歌) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 3\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners learn about family trees and can name grandma and grandpa.\n- Source: TB p15 | PB p15 | AB p15 | Audio 1.15\n- New Keywords: family tree, grandma, grandpa\n- Recycled Keywords: family, numbers, happy\n- Target Sentences: This is my (grandma). | (Grandma) is happy.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Build a simple family tree on the board with the teacher; add mum, dad, brother, sister, then grandma and grandpa.\n  2. Guided Practice — \"My tree\" speaking frame: learners point to a picture and say \"This is my (grandma / grandpa).\"; recycle He's / She's happy from Week 2.\n  3. Game / Application — Family-tree craft starter: each child begins a stick-figure tree (finish in Showcase week); teacher labels grandma / grandpa with support.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — revisit b, c, m through family words (b — brother / book; c — cat; m — mum / Matt); quick sound flash.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Great Big Book of Families (Mary Hoffman) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 2): Join in — read aloud; learners call out the repeated \"families ...\" pattern and find the grandma / grandpa / pet pages; connect to today's family tree.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: family tree, grandma, grandpa\n- Original Recycled Language: family, numbers, happy\n- Current Classification Result: New / recycled split carried from source.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - grandma / grandpa across home languages\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
