      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 3 · Day 3\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 3\n- Day: 3\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L9\n- Lesson Role: Cartoon story and consolidation of language in context\n\n## Day Focus\n- Understand vocabulary and language in the cartoon story The Friendly Family (fish, one of the family, Come here!, Here you are).\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Pets in our families (recycles pet, cat, friend, happy)\n- Song: Peekaboo, I Love You (Super Simple Songs, 11. 游戏儿歌) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 3\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners understand vocabulary and language in the context of the cartoon story.\n- Source: TB p16 | PB p16 | AB p16 | Audio 1.16, AB 1.13\n- New Keywords: fish, one of the family, Come here!, Here you are.\n- Recycled Keywords: colours, numbers, boy, cat, friend, girl, happy, pet\n- Target Sentences: Come here! | Here you are. | (The fish) is one of the family.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Watch / read The Friendly Family; pause on \"Come here!\" and \"Here you are.\"; learners act them out with a toy.\n  2. Guided Practice — \"One of the family\" : show a pet/fish picture, learners say \"one of the family\"; link to pets from Week 1.\n  3. Game / Application — Giving game: in pairs, one says \"Come here!\" and hands over a crayon/picture, the other says \"Here you are.\"; recycle happy and friend.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — b, c, m sound flash using cartoon words (c — cat; b — boy / book; m — mum); keep light.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Great Big Book of Families (Mary Hoffman) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 3): Connect — find the pet and fish pages in the big book; link \"one of the family\" to the many families and their animals in the book.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: fish, one of the family, Come here!, Here you are.\n- Original Recycled Language: colours, numbers, boy, cat, friend, girl, happy, pet\n- Current Classification Result: New / recycled split carried from source.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - imperative \"Come here! / Here you are.\" as polite routines\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
