      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 3 · Day 4\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 3\n- Day: 4\n- Day Type: Media Extend\n- Power Up Lesson: Media Extend 3\n- Lesson Role: EASTIE-added Media Extend — real-life screen input\n\n## Day Focus\n- Watch a short Peppa Pig clip about grandparents and connect it to grandma / grandpa and family trees.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Grandparents and family outings (recycles grandma, grandpa, family, happy)\n- Song: Peekaboo, I Love You (Super Simple Songs, 11. 游戏儿歌) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 3\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners watch a real-life cartoon clip and understand the gist (grandparents, family, being together).\n- Source: Peppa Pig, \"Grandpa Pig's Boat\" (Season 1, Episode 48, ~5 min) — Grandpa Pig, Granny Pig and the grandchildren go boating on the river; focuses on grandparents (grandpa / grandma) and family time. Focus words: grandma, grandpa, family, happy.\n- New Keywords: (none new — clip recycles Week 3 words)\n- Recycled Keywords: grandma, grandpa, family, happy, friend, Come here!\n- Target Sentences: This is my (grandpa). | (Grandpa) is happy.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Presentation / Input — Watch the clip; pause on Grandpa Pig and Granny Pig; learners point and say \"grandpa / grandma\".\n  2. Guided Practice — \"Who is in the boat?\" after viewing: learners name the family members; link to the Day 12 family tree.\n  3. Game / Application — \"My grandma / grandpa\" share: a few learners show or name a grandparent; connect to the big book of families.\n- Fallback if clip unavailable: Peppa Pig \"My Cousin Chloé\" (Season 1, Episode 28) for the cousin branch of the family tree, OR a Bluey grandparents episode.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — b, c, m sound flash (m — mum / Matt; b — boy / book; c — cat / cousin) using clip and family words.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Great Big Book of Families (Mary Hoffman) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 4): Own-life link — compare the boat family outing to our own grandparents; talk about a grandma or grandpa we love, like in the big book.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — Media Extend recycles unit language)\n- Original Recycled Language: grandma, grandpa, family, happy, friend, Come here!\n- Current Classification Result: Media Extend is input-only; all words already in Weeks 1–3.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - grandparent vocabulary across home languages\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
