      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 3 · Day 5\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 3\n- Day: 5\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L10\n- Lesson Role: Unit review and Mini-mission (poster activity)\n\n## Day Focus\n- Revise the whole unit's language and make a group \"Friends and Family\" poster for the Showcase wall.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Everything we know — quick recall of friends, family, he / she, happy, grandma / grandpa\n- Song: Peekaboo, I Love You (Super Simple Songs, 11. 游戏儿歌) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 3 (final sing of the week)\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners revise the language from the unit and contribute to a class poster.\n- Source: TB p17 | PB p17 | AB p17 | Audio 1.17, 1.18, AB 1.14\n- New Keywords: (none new — review lesson)\n- Recycled Keywords: unit language (man, woman, boy, girl, family, He's/She's, happy, school, teacher, grandma, grandpa, fish, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m sounds)\n- Target Sentences: (review of all unit sentences)\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Warm-up — Quick flash recall of unit words and he / she sentences.\n  2. Mini Mission — In groups of 3–4, each group draws one assigned word (e.g., book, five, yellow, girl, dad, grandma) on the class poster under \"Hello!\" / \"1 Friends and family\"; when finished each group stands, shows and says its word.\n  3. Display — Stick posters on the wall (\"Our English!\"); keep for the Week 4 Showcase. Teacher says \"Well done!\".\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — final b, c, m sound flash of the unit; these sounds carry into the Week 4 Showcase sound-hunt station.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: The Great Big Book of Families (Mary Hoffman) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 5): Retell — with teacher support, learners retell the big book in one line (\"Families are all different and all happy.\") and point to a favourite family page; close the week by singing the song together.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: None listed (review lesson)\n- Original Recycled Language: unit language\n- Current Classification Result: Review / consolidation of all prior weeks; no new graded vocabulary.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - full-unit recall confidence before Showcase\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
