      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 4 · Day 1\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 4\n- Day: 1\n- Day Type: Showcase\n- Power Up Lesson: Showcase L1\n- Lesson Role: Showcase launch and project planning\n\n## Day Focus\n- Launch the Week 4 Showcase: revisit the whole unit and plan a student-led \"Friends and Family Fair\".\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Our unit so far — what can we show? (recycles friends, family, he / she, happy, grandma / grandpa)\n- Song: See You Later, Alligator (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 4 (farewell / goodbye theme fits Showcase week)\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners recall the unit's language and, in groups of 3–4, choose one Showcase station to prepare over the week.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed, student-led) — builds on all of Weeks 1–3.\n- New Keywords: (none new — Showcase applies prior language)\n- Recycled Keywords: man, woman, boy, girl, family, He's/She's, happy, school, teacher, grandma, grandpa, fish, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m sounds\n- Target Sentences: This is my (family). | He's / She's (happy). | Come here!\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Launch — Picture recall of the unit: the café & playgroup from Week 2, the family tree & boat from Week 3, our friends & family from Week 1; sing See You Later, Alligator.\n  2. Plan — Form groups of 3–4; introduce the 4 Fair stations; each group picks ONE station to make and show:\n     - A. My Family Tree (from W3 family tree + W1 The Family Book)\n     - B. Our Class Family (from W2 playgroup/school + W4 All Are Welcome; includes a welcome-café corner using W3 menu/café words)\n     - C. Happy Faces (from W2 happy + W1 The More We Get Together)\n     - D. B-C-M Sound Hunt (from W3 phonics b/c/m; words include book, boy, cat, café, cup, mum, menu, man)\n  3. Prepare — Groups look at the Week 2 \"Happy Friends\" poster and Week 3 family-tree poster already on the wall for inspiration; teacher pre-teaches the sentence frames each station will use (see Delivery Plan).\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — b, c, m are one of the four stations (Sound Hunt); no new phoneme this week. Quick sound warm-up: teacher says /b/ /c/ /m/, children echo and show a thumbs-up.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: All Are Welcome (Alexandra Penfold) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 1): Picture walk — explore the cover and the welcoming school; predict who is welcome; notice children and families of all kinds.\n\n## Lesson Delivery Plan\n\n### Timing (≈50 min — adjust to your centre's schedule)\n- Circle Time: 10 min (includes phonics warm-up)\n- CLIL Class: 25 min (Launch 5 / Plan 12 / Prepare 8)\n- Story: 12 min\n- Transition buffer: 3 min\n\n### Materials to prep\n- Unit recall cards: café, playgroup, family tree, boat pictures (reuse from W1–W3)\n- 4 station choice cards (one per station, with a small icon)\n- Group allocation chart; the Week 2 \"Happy Friends\" poster and Week 3 family-tree/poster already on the wall\n- Sentence-frame strips per station, printed large (see scripts below)\n\n### Teacher scripts (key moments)\n- Launch: \"We learned a LOT! We met friends at the playgroup. We drew our family tree. Today we start our Fair — a party to show what we know!\"\n- Introduce stations (hold up each card): \"Station 1 — My Family Tree. Station 2 — Our Class Family. Station 3 — Happy Faces. Station 4 — B-C-M Sound Hunt. Which one will your group make?\"\n- Pre-teach frames (model + children echo):\n  - A Family Tree: \"This is my grandma.\" (point to photo)\n  - B Class Family: \"This is my friend. Come here!\"\n  - C Happy Faces: \"He's happy. / I am happy.\"\n  - D Sound Hunt: \"It starts with /b/ — book!\"\n- Chinese scaffold if stuck: \"这是我的奶奶。跟着老师说：This is my grandma.\"\n\n### Differentiation\n- Support: Teacher assigns the station; child echoes one keyword (\"grandma\") rather than the full sentence; uses point + name.\n- On-level: Uses the frame with one filled word (\"This is my grandma.\").\n- Stretch: Adds a second sentence (\"This is my grandma. She's happy.\") or invites a peer (\"Come here!\").\n\n### Success check (informal)\n- Group has chosen 1 station and can name it (\"We make the Family Tree!\").\n- Child can echo at least one target sentence after modeling.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — Showcase applies prior language)\n- Original Recycled Language: all unit language from Weeks 1–3\n- Current Classification Result: Showcase is application/creation; no new graded vocabulary.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - Group planning support (covered in Delivery Plan — teacher assigns station for Support level)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
