          "body": "- Lesson Outcome: Learners recall the unit's language and, in groups of 3–4, choose one Showcase station to prepare over the week.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed, student-led) — builds on all of Weeks 1–3.\n- New Keywords: (none new — Showcase applies prior language)\n- Recycled Keywords: man, woman, boy, girl, family, He's/She's, happy, school, teacher, grandma, grandpa, fish, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m sounds\n- Target Sentences: This is my (family). | He's / She's (happy). | Come here!\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Launch — Picture recall of the unit: the café & playgroup from Week 2, the family tree & boat from Week 3, our friends & family from Week 1; sing See You Later, Alligator.\n  2. Plan — Form groups of 3–4; introduce the 4 Fair stations; each group picks ONE station to make and show:\n     - A. My Family Tree (from W3 family tree + W1 The Family Book)\n     - B. Our Class Family (from W2 playgroup/school + W4 All Are Welcome; includes a welcome-café corner using W3 menu/café words)\n     - C. Happy Faces (from W2 happy + W1 The More We Get Together)\n     - D. B-C-M Sound Hunt (from W3 phonics b/c/m; words include book, boy, cat, café, cup, mum, menu, man)\n  3. Prepare — Groups look at the Week 2 \"Happy Friends\" poster and Week 3 family-tree poster already on the wall for inspiration; teacher pre-teaches the sentence frames each station will use (see Delivery Plan)."
