      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 4 · Day 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 4\n- Day: 2\n- Day Type: Showcase\n- Power Up Lesson: Showcase L2\n- Lesson Role: Showcase creation session 1\n\n## Day Focus\n- Groups create their Showcase artefacts using unit language with teacher support.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Making things together (recycles friend, happy, family)\n- Song: See You Later, Alligator (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 4\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Each child contributes to a group artefact and labels at least one item with a target sentence.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed) — creation session.\n- New Keywords: (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: family, grandma, grandpa, happy, boy, girl, He's/She's, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m\n- Target Sentences: This is my (grandma). | He's / She's (happy). | (It starts with) /b/.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Make — Groups work at their chosen station:\n     - A My Family Tree: stick / draw family members on the tree template; teacher writes name labels (grandma / grandpa / mum / dad / me).\n     - B Our Class Family: add own photo to the class board; in the welcome-café corner, role-play \"Here you are.\" with a toy cup (recycles W3 menu/café + W2 Come here!).\n     - C Happy Faces: draw a happy-face badge; teacher writes the child's name; sort happy vs. not-happy feeling cards.\n     - D B-C-M Sound Hunt: make / sort sound cards — /b/ book, boy; /c/ cat, café, cup; /m/ mum, menu, man.\n  2. Talk — While making, teacher models the frame and children echo + label their work (\"This is my grandma.\").\n  3. Check — Quick group check-in: each child holds up one item and says one sentence; teacher notes language used on a tick-list.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — Sound-Hunt group makes b/c/m cards (boy, book, cat, café, mum, menu); other groups spot these sounds in their own artefacts (e.g., \"mum\" on the family tree, \"cat\" on a happy-face drawing).\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: All Are Welcome (Alexandra Penfold) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 2): Join in — read aloud; learners join the repeated \"All are welcome here\" line and copy the welcoming gestures; connect to our class family.\n\n## Lesson Delivery Plan\n\n### Timing (≈50 min)\n- Circle Time: 8 min\n- CLIL Class: 30 min (Make 20 / Talk 7 / Check 3)\n- Story: 12 min\n\n### Materials to prep (per station)\n- A: A3 tree template (pre-drawn trunk + branches), family photos from home (sent in earlier) or crayons, name-label stickers, glue.\n- B: class board + each child's photo, toy cups/plates, \"welcome\" banner.\n- C: blank badge circles, small mirrors (to see own face), feeling cards (happy / sad / tired), markers.\n- D: sound-card blanks, picture prompts (book, boy, cat, café, cup, mum, menu, man), letter cards b / c / m.\n\n### Teacher scripts\n- Open making: \"Today we MAKE our Fair! Station A — draw your family. Station B — our class family. Station C — happy faces. Station D — sound hunt.\"\n- Model + echo (at a group): \"This is my grandma.\" (child echoes) \"He's happy!\"\n- Café role play (Station B): child hands over a toy cup → Teacher: \"Here you are!\" → child echoes \"Here you are!\"\n- Chinese scaffold: \"把照片贴上去。说：This is my grandma.\"\n\n### Differentiation\n- Support: Pre-written name labels; child points + says the keyword (\"grandma\"); teacher completes the sentence.\n- On-level: Uses the frame with one filled word (\"This is my grandma.\").\n- Stretch: Labels 2+ items; adds \"She's happy.\"; Sound-Hunt child finds a third word.\n\n### Success check\n- Each child has a partial artefact and has labeled ≥1 item with a target sentence (echoed or independent).\n- Teacher tick-list: child name → station → sentence attempted.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — creation applies prior language)\n- Original Recycled Language: all unit language from Weeks 1–3\n- Current Classification Result: Creation session; recycled language only.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - artefact-language labelling (covered in Delivery Plan — teacher writes labels, child echoes)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
