      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 4 · Day 3\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 4\n- Day: 3\n- Day Type: Showcase\n- Power Up Lesson: Showcase L3\n- Lesson Role: Showcase rehearsal\n\n## Day Focus\n- Rehearse presenting the Showcase artefacts using simple sentences and polite routines.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Practising our lines (recycles Come here!, Here you are., happy)\n- Song: See You Later, Alligator (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 4\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners rehearse a short presentation of their Showcase station with support.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed) — rehearsal session.\n- New Keywords: (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: family, grandma, grandpa, happy, He's/She's, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m, friend\n- Target Sentences: This is my (family tree). | He's / She's (happy). | Come here! | Here you are.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Rehearse — Each group practises showing their artefact and saying 1–2 sentences; teacher gives gentle prompts (\"What is this? Say: This is my…\").\n  2. Peer listen — Groups take turns in a low-stakes rehearsal; classmates respond \"Happy!\" or clap for each other (recycle happy).\n  3. Polish — Groups decide who says what; teacher helps with the Sound-Hunt and family-tree labels.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — Sound-Hunt group rehearses calling initial sounds /b/ /c/ /m/ for their cards; other groups listen and hold up the matching letter card.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: All Are Welcome (Alexandra Penfold) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 3): Connect — link the book's \"all welcome\" message to our Fair: every group's work is welcome on the wall, just like every family in the book.\n\n## Lesson Delivery Plan\n\n### Timing (≈50 min)\n- Circle Time: 8 min\n- CLIL Class: 28 min (Rehearse 14 / Peer listen 8 / Polish 6)\n- Story: 12 min\n- Transition buffer: 2 min\n\n### Materials to prep\n- The half-finished artefacts from Day 17, laid out at each station\n- A \"stage\" spot (a small rug / a paper microphone prop) so children know where to stand\n- Letter cards b / c / m for the Sound-Hunt listeners\n- Clap / \"Happy!\" prompt card for the peer-listen step\n\n### Teacher scripts\n- Start rehearsal: \"Today we practise! Group A, come to the stage. Show us your tree. Say: This is my family tree.\"\n- Gentle prompt when a child is stuck: \"Point to grandma. Now say: This is my grandma.\" (then \"Good! She's happy!\")\n- Peer listen: \"Everyone — when a friend finishes, say 'Happy!' or clap. Ready? Go!\"\n- Chinese scaffold: \"站到前面来，说：This is my family tree.\"\n\n### Differentiation\n- Support: Holds the artefact and says one keyword; teacher says the full sentence and child echoes; stands with a buddy.\n- On-level: Says 1 sentence independently (\"This is my family tree.\").\n- Stretch: Says 2 sentences (\"This is my family tree. She's happy.\") or invites a peer (\"Come here!\").\n\n### Success check\n- Every group has run through its presentation once.\n- Each child attempts ≥1 sentence (echoed or independent) during the rehearsal.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — rehearsal applies prior language)\n- Original Recycled Language: all unit language from Weeks 1–3\n- Current Classification Result: Rehearsal; recycled language only.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - presentation confidence (covered in Delivery Plan — buddy standing + gentle prompts)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
