      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 4 · Day 4\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 4\n- Day: 4\n- Day Type: Showcase\n- Power Up Lesson: Showcase L4\n- Lesson Role: Showcase dress rehearsal and peer feedback\n\n## Day Focus\n- Run a full dress rehearsal of the Fair and give friendly peer feedback before the final day.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Getting ready to show (recycles friend, happy, school)\n- Song: See You Later, Alligator (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 4\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners perform a full run-through and respond to simple peer feedback.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed) — dress rehearsal.\n- New Keywords: (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: family, grandma, grandpa, happy, He's/She's, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m, friend, school, teacher\n- Target Sentences: This is my (...). | He's / She's (happy). | Come here! | Here you are.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Run-through — Groups present in order as they will on the final day; teacher times and supports transitions between groups.\n  2. Feedback — After each group, the class gives one happy comment (\"I like your family tree!\"); teacher models kind feedback.\n  3. Fix — Groups make small improvements (a missing label, a clearer sentence) before the final.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — Sound-Hunt cards finalised; all groups spot b/c/m somewhere in the Fair (e.g., \"book\" on Sound Hunt, \"mum\" on family tree, \"cat\" on a happy face).\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: All Are Welcome (Alexandra Penfold) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 4): Own-life link — talk about a time we welcomed someone new (like the book, like George's first day in Week 2); connect to belonging in our class.\n\n## Lesson Delivery Plan\n\n### Timing (≈50 min)\n- Circle Time: 8 min\n- CLIL Class: 28 min (Run-through 16 / Feedback 7 / Fix 5)\n- Story: 12 min\n- Transition buffer: 2 min\n\n### Materials to prep\n- All finished artefacts laid out at stations\n- Feedback sentence-stem card: \"I like your ___!\" (with picture cues)\n- A simple timer / visual countdown for transitions\n- \"Well done!\" stamps or stickers for the final day prep\n\n### Teacher scripts\n- Start: \"Today is our DRESS rehearsal — like the real show, but just us. Group A first!\"\n- Kind feedback model: \"Tell them one thing you like. I like your happy face!\" (child echoes stem)\n- Transition: \"Time! Thank you Group A. Group B, you're next — come to the stage.\"\n- Chinese scaffold: \"说一句你喜欢的：I like your family tree!\"\n\n### Differentiation\n- Support: Gives a thumbs-up or points to the part they like; teacher voices the sentence (\"Tommy likes your tree!\").\n- On-level: Uses the stem with one noun (\"I like your family tree!\").\n- Stretch: Adds a reason (\"I like your family tree — it's big!\") or asks a question to the presenting group.\n\n### Success check\n- Full run-through completed in order, with a transition between every group.\n- Each group receives ≥1 peer comment and notes one small fix to make.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — dress rehearsal applies prior language)\n- Original Recycled Language: all unit language from Weeks 1–3\n- Current Classification Result: Dress rehearsal; recycled language only.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - kind peer feedback (covered in Delivery Plan — stem card + teacher model)\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
