      "sourceMarkdown": "# K1 Unit 1 · Week 4 · Day 5\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K1\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Friends and Family\n- Week: 4\n- Day: 5\n- Day Type: Showcase\n- Power Up Lesson: Showcase L5\n- Lesson Role: Final Showcase presentation and celebration\n\n## Day Focus\n- Present the Friends and Family Fair to the class (and families), celebrate, and close the unit with a farewell song.\n\n## Displayed Content\n\n### Circle Time\n- Topic: Our big day! (recycles friend, family, happy, school)\n- Song: See You Later, Alligator (Super Simple Songs, 05. 社交启蒙) — one song per week, shared across all 5 days of Week 4 (final sing — farewell to the unit)\n\n### CLIL Class\n- Lesson Outcome: Learners present their Showcase station and celebrate the unit's learning.\n- Source: Showcase Week (EASTIE-designed) — final presentation.\n- New Keywords: (none new)\n- Recycled Keywords: family, grandma, grandpa, happy, He's/She's, Come here!, Here you are., b/c/m, friend, school, teacher, man, woman, boy, girl, They're\n- Target Sentences: This is my (family). | He's / She's (happy). | They're (my friends). | Come here! | Here you are. | (It starts with) /b/.\n- Activities and Games:\n  1. Present — Groups present their station to the class / invited families; each child says at least one sentence; teacher supports.\n  2. Celebrate — Class walks the \"Fair\", looks at every poster (including the Week 2/3 posters), and says \"Well done!\"; sing See You Later, Alligator.\n  3. Close — Teacher praises effort; point back to the unit purpose \"Talk about friends and family.\"; artefacts go home or stay on the wall.\n\n### Phonics\n- Content: Consolidation — final b, c, m sound moment at the Sound-Hunt station; phonics continue in later units.\n\n### Story\n- Book / Story: All Are Welcome (Alexandra Penfold) — picture-book, one book per week\n- Daily Focus (Day 5): Retell — with teacher support, learners retell the book in one line (\"All are welcome in our class.\"); close the unit by singing the farewell song together.\n\n## Lesson Delivery Plan\n\n### Timing (≈60 min — this is the event day; split into two 30-min blocks if needed)\n- Circle Time (welcome): 8 min\n- CLIL Class (Present + Celebrate): 35 min (Present 22 / Celebrate 13)\n- Story (retell + farewell): 12 min\n- Transition / photo buffer: 5 min\n\n### Materials to prep\n- Invitations sent home earlier; chairs/standing space for families\n- All station artefacts laid out as a \"Fair\" (4 tables / wall spots)\n- \"Well done!\" stamps or certificates; a class photo plan\n- Farewell song lyric card for See You Later, Alligator\n\n### Teacher scripts\n- Welcome families: \"Welcome to our Friends and Family Fair! Today the children show what they learned. This is my family — let's watch!\"\n- During presentation (support): \"Show your tree. Say: This is my grandma.\" → \"Wonderful! She's happy!\"\n- Café corner (Station B): child serves a toy cup → \"Here you are!\"; family claps.\n- Close: \"We can all talk about friends and family now. Well done, everyone! Let's sing our song.\"\n- Chinese scaffold: \"请爸爸妈妈看，说：This is my family.\"\n\n### Differentiation\n- Support: Presents with a buddy; says one keyword or echoes teacher's sentence; family member can stand with them.\n- On-level: Says ≥1 full sentence independently.\n- Stretch: Says 2 sentences or welcomes a family member (\"Come here! This is my mum.\").\n\n### Success check\n- Every child presents ≥1 sentence at the Fair.\n- Class completes the celebration walk + farewell song; artefacts acknowledged.\n\n## Source Audit\n- Original New Language: (none — final Showcase applies prior language)\n- Original Recycled Language: all unit language from Weeks 1–3\n- Current Classification Result: Final Showcase; recycled language only.\n\n## Review Issues\n- Needs Extension:\n  - none — unit complete\n- Source Issues:\n  - None for this day.\n",
